  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bringing communities together and empowering vulnerable children in border areas through football in Tajikistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project promotes inclusion, resilience, and cross-border cohesion by expanding access to safe football infrastructure and structured, football-based engagement for children in Tajikistan&apos;s border regions. Children and youth in these areas face multiple risks linked to geographic isolation, economic hardship, border tensions, and limited access to safe recreational spaces, increasing their vulnerability to social exclusion, exploitation, and harmful coping mechanisms. In response, the initiative implemented jointly by IOM Tajikistan and the Tajikistan Football Federation, funded by UEFA Foundation for Children, will construct or rehabilitate inclusive football fields in selected border communities, creating safe spaces for children, including girls and children with disabilities. These facilities will serve as hubs for football activities, cross-border tournaments, and community events that bring together children from different backgrounds, including Tajik, Kyrgyz, and Afghan communities. The project integrates football with life skills development and child-focused mental health and psychosocial support, fostering confidence, teamwork, and social interaction. It also promotes community ownership through participatory planning and maintenance mechanisms. By leveraging football as a platform for inclusion and dialogue, the project aims to strengthen social cohesion, reduce tensions, and empower vulnerable children, contributing to long-term peacebuilding and community resilience in fragile border areas.</narrative>
  </description>
